      "title": "One Nation vows to cut migration by 750,000 amid warnings move would damage economy",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/one-nation-new-migration-plan-cut-750000-aged-care-impact-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>New immigration policy has attracted bipartisan condemnation, with Labor warning it would damage construction, healthcare and agriculture</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/14/australia-politics-live-question-time-electric-vehicles-auction-rates-housing-crisis-albanese-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One Nation says it will cut the number of temporary migrants in Australia by more than 750,000 over three years, targeting international students and family members of skilled migrants in a “net-negative” plan.</p><p>But the business and agriculture sectors have warned the plan would badly hurt the economy and weaken essential services, without lifting living standards for Australians.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/one-nation-new-migration-plan-cut-750000-aged-care-impact-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-14T02:04:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australian politics live: Hastie urges deal with US to get AI model; Taylor says Hanson’s comments on PM’s mother ‘off limits’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/14/australia-politics-live-question-time-electric-vehicles-auction-rates-housing-crisis-albanese-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Hanson’s comments on Albanese’s mother ‘gratuitous and unnecessary’: Hume</strong></p><p><strong>Jane Hume</strong> has joined the pile on, blasting <strong>Pauline Hanson</strong> for her comments about <strong>Anthony Albanese’s</strong> mother.</p><p>I think that these comments were gratuitous and unnecessary. And the idea that you would disparage people that have grown up in social housing, I think, is a little distasteful. I mean, it doubles down on the fact that Senator Hanson has also disrespected our veteran community with her atrocious comments about Andrew Hastie in that cartoon. Calling a veteran a traitor, I think, is possibly the worst thing you can do.</p><p><strong>But this does seem to be a common theme in One Nation now, that sort of unnecessarily provocative rhetoric.</strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/14/australia-politics-live-question-time-electric-vehicles-auction-rates-housing-crisis-albanese-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-14T01:50:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "Motorcyclist’s death reignites debate over potholes on Victoria’s ‘deteriorating’ roads",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/motorcyclist-dies-pothole-trawalla-ballarat-victoria-roads",
      "description": "<p>Coalition says potholes must be fixed ‘as a matter of urgency’ after 71-year-old crashed and died on Western Highway at Trawalla, west of Ballarat, on Sunday</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/14/australia-politics-live-question-time-electric-vehicles-auction-rates-housing-crisis-albanese-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Emergency services were called to Trawalla, west of Ballarat, shortly before 1pm on Sunday after reports a motorcycle had struck a pothole.</p><p>The 71-year-old rider, from Ballarat, died at the scene after reportedly losing control on the Western Highway, near Trawalla Road.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/motorcyclist-dies-pothole-trawalla-ballarat-victoria-roads\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-14T00:44:34"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mary Gaudron, first female judge of Australia’s high court, dies aged 83",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/sep/14/mary-gaudron-dies-aged-83-death-first-female-judge-australia-high-court",
      "description": "<p>Legal pioneer remembered as an advocate for equality and champion of women in the workplace</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/14/australia-politics-live-question-time-electric-vehicles-auction-rates-housing-crisis-albanese-labor-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Mary Gaudron, the first woman appointed to the high court of Australia, has been honoured for her contributions to the legal landscape after her death at the age of 83.</p><p>Gaudron was appointed to the high court in 1987, aged 44, and served until 2003.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/law/2026/sep/14/mary-gaudron-dies-aged-83-death-first-female-judge-australia-high-court\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
